sequenceDiagram
  participant C as Caller
  participant R as Ravel CLI
  participant W as Rhai worker
  participant F as Token file
  participant K as Runner
  participant M as Claude Code, confined
  C->>R: start-session --confine
  R->>R: Check each tokenHandoffs record in the settings
  R->>R: Resolve the declared path and the real path of each token file once
  R->>R: Refuse a second link, or a skill source over a protected path, before capture
  R->>R: Prepare confinement and refuse a grant over a protected path
  R->>W: Evaluate the request
  W-->>R: Selection that names claude-code
  R->>F: Check expires, then resolve the declared path again
  R->>F: Open the protected real path, with no link in the last component
  R->>F: Check type, owner, mode, one link and size on the open file
  R->>F: Read the open file once, at most 4,097 bytes
  alt A check or the read fails
    R-->>C: token_handoff_unavailable, exit 3, nothing launched
  else Every check passes
    R->>R: Socket pair: write, shut down and close Ravel's end
    R->>K: Launch with the other end in the descriptor list
    K->>K: Grant each path in its checked form, refuse one that resolves elsewhere
    K->>M: Keep only the listed socket open across exec
    M->>M: Read the socket, close it and remove the variable
  end
